Package: rafe
Type: Package
Title: Decision-Aligned Forecast Evaluation and Moment Correction
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Sebastian", "Stöckl", email = "sebastian.stoeckl@uni.li",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Evaluates return forecasts by the economic damage their errors
    cause, rather than by their size. Implements the risk-adjusted forecast
    error (RAFE), the operator-norm covariance forecast error (C-RAFE), and
    their combination into an upper bound on the Sharpe-ratio gap of a
    plug-in mean-variance portfolio (T-RAFE), as established in Salcher,
    Stoeckl and Hanke (2026) <doi:10.1002/for.70134>. Conventional accuracy
    measures such as root mean squared error weight every asset equally,
    while a portfolio optimiser does not; these metrics reweight forecast
    errors by the risk metric the decision actually uses. Also provides
    moment-correction estimators acting on the two channels of the bound,
    namely positive-part James-Stein mean shrinkage in the risk-whitened
    space and eigenvalue-floor covariance cleaning, with shrinkage intensity
    and floor selected on an inner-validation split.
